main.personas:
User Characters (player-controlled):
```json
[
  {
    "name": "Ardan Kell",
    "description": "Sex: Male A\nge: 33 Race: Human (city-born, low quarter)\n\nAppearance: Six foot even, broad-shouldered, going gray at the temples a decade early. A boxer's nose broken twice and set once. Dark stubble he keeps at three days regardless of circumstance. Wears a watchman's coat with the insignia cut off — the stitch-holes are still visible, and he knows they are. Carries a plain arming sword, a truncheon he is more comfortable with, and a copper watch-whistle on a cord that he has never explained and never removed.\n\nBackground: Fourteen years in the city watch, four of them as a sergeant, ending the night he filed a report on a captain who had been selling passage through the harbor gate. The report vanished. So did the captain's problem. Ardan kept his life and lost his post, his pension, and most of the people he called friends. He takes charter work now because it is the only honest version of the job he knows how to do. Reads people well, reads rooms better, and is quietly appalled by how much more the Ninth Kestrel gets away with than the Watch ever did.\n\nGear & abilities: Plain arming sword, a watchman's truncheon he's far more comfortable with, manacles, and the copper whistle. No magic. Trained interrogation, street tracking, and twenty years of knowing when a room is about to go bad."
  }
]
```

